  "@settingsDialogClearHistoryConfirm": {
    "description": "⚠️ **`Clear`, not `OK`, and not `Delete`** — it names the object. And § 4 (Empty — no data) forbids the dialog opening at all when the count is zero, so a reader is never asked to confirm destroying nothing."
  },
  "@settingsDialogClearHistoryTitle": {
    "description": "⚠️ **The count is in the TITLE**, not the body. This dialog's one job is to say how much is about to be destroyed, and a title is what a reader reads before they read anything else. `3-7`'s Loading state exists only for the COUNT this sentence waits on.",
